{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You have circled this mountain long enough.</b> Many say that this verse pierces and descends to the abyss and contains an allusion for the hour and for the generations. The meaning of this circling is that they would go round and round the vineyard of YHWH of Hosts but not draw near — for many days Israel wandered and journeyed around it, and no strength was given to Israel over it until 'the tread of a foot,' until there would come the one of whom it is said: ״וְעָמְדוּ רַגְלָיו בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא עַל הַר הַזֵּיתִים״ (Zechariah 14:4). And all the while that Israel go round and round, it is said to them: ״פְּנוּ לָכֶם צָפוֹנָה״ — and they expounded this: if the hour of Esau has arrived, hide yourselves (Deuteronomy Rabbah 1:19)." "And the meaning of this hiding seems to me to be: if the Jewish man finds in this exile of Seir some small success there, then let him conceal and hide everything from Esau — for there is no nation that is enraged with jealousy against Israel like Esau, for according to their thinking, everything in their hands is plunder from the blessing of Jacob our father, who took his blessings from Esau by deception. And so Jacob commanded his sons: ״לָמָּה תִתְרָאוּ״ (Genesis 42:1) — Rashi explained: before the children of Ishmael and Esau, as though you are sated. For both of them hold that Isaac robbed the success of Ishmael, and Jacob robbed the success of Esau through scheming. Therefore he commanded specifically concerning Esau: ״פְּנוּ לָכֶם צָפוֹנָה״ — so that he would not be envious of you. And this is the opposite of what Israel do in these generations in the lands of their enemies: for whoever has a hundred shows himself off in garments of splendor and in stately and grand houses as though he had several thousands, and provokes the nations themselves, and transgresses what was said: ״פְּנוּ לָכֶם צָפוֹנָה״. And this practice is widespread among many of our people's children, and it is what brings about all the affliction that has found us. And the discerning will understand to take instruction."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:11:04.106299643Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}